            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request updates the MQA logits chunking logic in `dsa_indexer.py` to empty the PyTorch CUDA cache and re-evaluate free memory when chunking is deemed necessary. The reviewer identified a potential performance bottleneck where a cached low budget value could trigger expensive `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` calls on every subsequent forward pass. They provided a code suggestion to invalidate the cached budget after clearing the cache and re-evaluate the budget properly.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The [consumer version of Gemini Code Assist on GitHub](https://developers.google.com/gemini-code-assist/docs/review-repo-code) is being sunset. Starting **June 18, 2026**, new organization installations will be blocked, and all code review activity will officially cease on **July 17, 2026**.\n> For more details on the timeline and next steps, please review the [Help Documentation](https://developers.google.com/gemini-code-assist/docs/deprecations/consumer-code-review).",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nIf `_get_mqa_logits_budget_bytes` caches a low budget value due to temporary memory pressure from PyTorch's caching allocator, subsequent calls will always trigger `need_chunk = True` initially. This forces `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` to be called on every single forward pass, which is extremely expensive and defeats the purpose of caching the budget to avoid host synchronization.\n\nTo fix this, we should invalidate/pop the cached budget for the device after calling `torch.cuda.empty_cache()`, and then re-evaluate the budget using `_get_mqa_logits_budget_bytes` so that the updated higher budget is cached for future steps.\n\n```suggestion\n        if need_chunk:\n            # Return unused blocks held by PyTorch's caching allocator to CUDA,\n            # then re-evaluate with the refreshed amount of free device memory.\n            # This does not release memory occupied by live tensors.\n            free_mem_before_empty_cache, _ = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(device_index)\n            torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n            self._mqa_logits_budget_bytes.pop(device_index, None)\n            logits_budget_bytes = self._get_mqa_logits_budget_bytes(device_index)\n            need_chunk = logits_bytes > logits_budget_bytes\n            free_mem, _ = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(device_index)\n            logger.info(\n                \"DSA MQA logits released unused PyTorch CUDA cache: \"\n                \"free memory %.2f GiB -> %.2f GiB, logits %.2f GiB, \"\n                \"need_chunk=%s\",\n                free_mem_before_empty_cache / (1024**3),\n                free_mem / (1024**3),\n                logits_bytes / (1024**3),\n                need_chunk,\n            )\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-19T07:55:08Z",
                  "databaseId": 3610149005,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -1097,6 +1097,25 @@ def _should_chunk_mqa_logits(\n         logits_budget_bytes = self._get_mqa_logits_budget_bytes(device_index)\n \n         need_chunk = logits_bytes > logits_budget_bytes\n+        if need_chunk:\n+            # Return unused blocks held by PyTorch's caching allocator to CUDA,\n+            # then re-evaluate with the refreshed amount of free device memory.\n+            # This does not release memory occupied by live tensors.\n+            free_mem_before_empty_cache, _ = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(device_index)\n+            torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n+            free_mem, total_mem = torch.cuda.mem_get_info(device_index)\n+            need_chunk = (logits_bytes * 2 > free_mem) or (\n+                logits_bytes > total_mem * self._MQA_LOGITS_TOTAL_MEM_FRACTION\n+            )\n+            logger.info(\n+                \"DSA MQA logits released unused PyTorch CUDA cache: \"\n+                \"free memory %.2f GiB -> %.2f GiB, logits %.2f GiB, \"\n+                \"need_chunk=%s\",\n+                free_mem_before_empty_cache / (1024**3),\n+                free_mem / (1024**3),\n+                logits_bytes / (1024**3),\n+                need_chunk,\n+            )",
